VERDICT
==============================================================================
  [1] gap(T) = gap(carre-du-champ form in L^2(vacuum)) : EXACT (machine precision).
  [2] discrete vs continuous time normalisation: factor (1-x)/(-log x), computable.
  [3] the GRADIENT form needs the metric matched to the kinetic term; matched, it equals
      the gap (ratio -> 1 as eps -> 0); at beta=2.5 with the unit metric it is off by a
      fixed factor printed above.
  [4] the full-chain Poincare constant is STRICTLY below the vacuum-slice constant.
  [5] the subspace projection never lowers the constant (gauge-invariance analog).
  [6] the LSI constant is strictly weaker than Poincare with an unbounded loss.
